        "v": 5,
        "title": "Extract code-map into standalone package",
        "summary": "The `common` package's `codemap` subsystem is extracted into a new `packages/code-map` package. This isolates tree-sitter dependencies and query files, removing them from `common`'s build and dependency list. The npm-app and test packages are updated to reference the new package via tsconfig paths and build scripts.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T19:00:49.634Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The code-scanning and code-understanding helpers that the app uses to read your project files have been moved into their own dedicated folder, so they no longer travel bundled inside the main shared toolkit. If you looked at the project layout today, you'd see a new top-level folder holding those helpers, and the shared toolkit's build steps and project wiring now skip over the scanning tools entirely. This is live now, so users running the app get the same scanning behavior, but the engineering team can now maintain the scanning tools independently from the rest of the shared toolkit.",
