        "title": "detectInstaller uses which manicode",
        "summary": "detectInstaller in npm-app/src/update-manicode.ts now resolves the binary path via `which manicode` instead of inspecting `process.execPath`. This ensures the installer detection logic checks the actual executable location rather than the Node.js runtime path. The change affects the update mechanism within the npm-app package.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T19:00:27.751Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When your computer asks itself which tool should have installed the program, it now looks at where the program actually lives on your machine instead of guessing from the path to the background helper that runs the install. That small fix makes the wrong-installer guess less likely, so the update step that happens after this runs will more often pick the same installer you originally used. The tooling already shipped this behavior, so it is live for the next update check your copy runs.",
