        "v": 5,
        "title": "env loader switches path resolution from ENVIRONMENT to RENDER",
        "summary": "backend, common, and web env loaders now resolve DOTENV_PATH using process.env.RENDER === 'true' instead of checking ENVIRONMENT === 'local'. This decouples file location logic from the environment name, allowing local-style relative paths on Render regardless of the ENVIRONMENT value. Affects backend/src/env.mjs, common/src/db/env.mjs, and web/src/env.mjs. Non-Render deployments continue reading secrets from /etc/secrets.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T18:58:39.377Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When the software starts up, it now decides where to look for your secret key files based on whether it is running on the Render cloud platform, rather than guessing from the name of the environment. This means deployments hosted on Render will correctly read their configuration from a relative folder instead of a system secrets directory, while all other hosting providers continue reading from the system secrets directory as before. You would not see a visible difference unless your deployment is on Render, where configuration loading should work more reliably.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "133e89fe4317",
        "at": "2026-09-18T00:51:55.625Z"
      },
